{
  "contract": "# Ordinary empty UI wire v1 (source/pure only)\n\nThis is the single wire definition shared by Python/C++/Dart. No runtime approval.\nAll objects are closed: missing/extra/duplicate keys reject. UTF-8, no BOM, ASCII\nJSON escapes, lexicographic ASCII key order, no insignificant whitespace, integer\nnumbers only (no bool-as-int, float, exponent, -0), final single LF for files and\nphase lines. SHA256 lowercase hex hashes the actual complete bytes, including LF.\nCanonical JSON strings use JSON escaping; slash is not escaped; non-ASCII uses\nlowercase four-digit UTF-16 escapes (surrogate pairs where necessary).\n\nTypes: H=64 lowercase hex; ID=16 lowercase hex volume serial + ':' + 16 lowercase\nhex file index; SID=actual owner SID string; P=normalized physical long DOS path\n(backslashes, no trailing slash); runId=`ui-`+8 lowercase hex; attempt=32 lowercase\nhex; desktopNonce=`ShiyuIso_`+32 lowercase hex. All integer values 0..2^53-1;\npid/tid/HWND/seq are positive. creationFileTime is a positive decimal **string**,\nno leading zeros. No path supplied by caller grants authority.\nNative converts uintptr_t HWND only after exact <=2^53-1 check; out-of-range\nrejects, never truncates or passes through float/JavaScript Number conversion.\nCanonical strings reject isolated surrogate code units; valid pairs encode normally.\nThis startup-only codec does not alter existing learning snapshot v4 raw UTF8.\nP preserves actual case returned by GetFinalPathNameByHandleW (normalized DOS),\nremoving the local \\\\?\\ prefix then GetLongPathNameW; never lowercase/re-case it.\nRemove non-root trailing backslash. All scope/digest/anchor comparisons use this\nexact physical spelling; a path alias never substitutes its shorter text.\n\nCLI exactly: --shiyu-ui-validation=ordinary-empty-ui,\n--shiyu-ui-run=runId, --shiyu-ui-attempt=attempt,\n--shiyu-ui-desktop=desktopNonce, --shiyu-ui-silent=true.\nAll five required once; unknown validation namespace/legacy validation flags reject.\n\nAnchor fields: protocol:1, purpose:\"ordinary-empty-ui-anchor\", ownerSid:SID,\nworkspacePath:P, basePath:P, workspaceIdentity:ID, baseIdentity:ID,\nsourceSha256:H, bundleSha256:H, commonSha256:H. <=2048 bytes.\nIntent fields: protocol:1, role:\"ordinary-empty-ui\", runId, attempt, desktopNonce,\nownerSid:SID, workspaceIdentity:ID, baseIdentity:ID, runIdentity:ID,\nprofileLeaf:\"profile\", stdoutIdentity:ID, stderrIdentity:ID,\nanchorSha256:H, imageSha256:H, bundleSha256:H, commonSha256:H. <=8192 bytes.\nParent creates anchor/intent/stdout/stderr; profile must not yet exist.\n\nrootScope=SHA256(canonical JSON array bytes **without LF**):\n[\"ordinary-empty-scope:1\",ownerSid,workspaceIdentity,baseIdentity,runIdentity,\n normalizedPhysicalProfile,attempt].\nownerScope=SHA256(canonical JSON array bytes without LF):[rootScope,trustedOwnerId].\n\nC0 fields: protocol:1, role:\"ordinary-empty-ui\", runId, attempt, desktopNonce,\nrootScope:H, appPid:int, creationFileTime:decimal-string, imageSha256:H,\nbundleSha256:H. C adds ownerScope:H, mainIsolateId:nonempty VM main isolate id.\ncontextHash=SHA256(canonical C object bytes **without LF**).\n\nPrefix exactly ASCII `SHIYU_UI_PHASE `; complete line <=4096 bytes, cumulative\nprotocol <=65536, raw stdout <=262144. Other stdout lines retained privately and\nignored as protocol. Partial prefix/JSON line stays pending, never readiness.\nMalformed/duplicate/unknown phase or wrong role/context fails sticky.\nEach phase is {phase:string,context:C0,proof:object}; C0 is identical throughout.\nNative phase order: native-gate-accepted then native-window-created; Dart ready\nmust follow gate, may interleave window-created. Each phase occurs once.\n\nnative-gate-accepted proof closed fields: nativeTid:int, desktopName:string,\nstation:\"WinSta0\", grantedAccess:int, intentSha256:H, workspaceIdentity:ID,\nbaseIdentity:ID, runIdentity:ID, stdoutIdentity:ID, stderrIdentity:ID.\ndesktopName must equal context.desktopNonce; access must contain 0x83 and no bits\noutside 0x20087. These are actual reads, parent verifies retained process identity.\nnative-window-created proof: mainHwnd:int, mainTid:int,\nwindowClass:\"FLUTTER_RUNNER_WIN32_WINDOW\".\nordinary-shell-frame-ready proof: nativeGateLineSha256:H, ownerScope:H,\nrootMatches:true, g1Held:true, shellMounted:true, frameRendered:true,\nsilent:true, frameCount:positive-int, viewportWidth:int, viewportHeight:int,\ndprMilli:positive-int, bandLeft:int, bandTop:int, bandWidth:int, bandHeight:int.\nViewport/band coordinates are physical pixel integers; dprMilli is round(DPR*1000).\nThe rounded DPR is metadata only, never permission to rescale/crop/repaint pixels.\nEmpty/loading facts remain actual status evidence, not ready assertions.\nowner-drained proof: ownerScope:H, stopConfirmed:true, storesDrained:true,\nstoresClosed:true, authorityReleased:true. native-loop-ended proof:\nmainHwnd:int, mainAbsent:true, messageLoopExit:0. Failed startup never forges these.\n\nRPC methods only ext.shiyu.validation.status and ext.shiyu.validation.close.\nstatus request: {contextHash:H,seq:positive-int,phase:\"observe\"}.\nclose request: {contextHash:H,seq:positive-int,phase:\"close\",grantSha256:H}.\nVM service query transports values as strings; seq is canonical decimal, extension\nparses exact decimal integer and rejects malformed/unknown parameters. Payload\ncanonical digest uses numeric seq as above. seq starts 1 and increments by one\nacross both methods; never retry. Exact reply: {method,contextHash,seq,childPhase,\nobservedAtMicros:decimal-string,facts:object}; facts schema is per method and is\nnot caller authority. close facts exactly {accepted:true}; no completed boolean.\nstatus facts exactly {ownerReady:bool,g1Held:bool,loading:bool,learningCount:int,\nmaterialCount:int,hasSelection:bool,hasSource:bool,frameCount:int,\nviewportWidth:int,viewportHeight:int,dprMilli:int,bandLeft:int,bandTop:int,\nbandWidth:int,bandHeight:int}. Failed sessions reject observe with typed failure;\nretention snapshot remains private diagnostics, not a passing status response.\n\nclose.grant canonical file <=4096 bytes: {protocol:1,role:\"ordinary-empty-ui\",\ncontext:C,contextHash:H,grantId:32lowerhex,seq:positive-int,phase:\"close\",\nobserverReceiptSha256:H}. It is CreateNew/flush/close once, only after pending\nsettles, same retained hThread is OS terminal exit0, joined and CloseHandle\nconfirmed. No observerDone input. Child validates physical run/private plain file,\nexact raw digest/context/seq, consumes before await, starts actual Owner exit once.\nTimeout/EOF/late reply is sticky unknown; neither retry nor green restoration.\n\nState: guarded -> owner-ready -> shell-frame-ready -> observing -> close-accepted\n-> draining -> native-closing; failed sticky side path. Status observe only in\nshell-frame-ready/observing. Close only after ready+qualified reader termination.\nDefault worker remains through actual App and reader OS terminals/handle closes.\n\nFixed native readonly channel, two methods only, request null, response canonical\nASCII JSON string (no LF); no file path arguments, Bind or resource acquisition.\n`startupValidationProof`: {protocol:1,c0:C0,workspacePath:P,basePath:P,runPath:P,\nprofilePath:P,workspaceIdentity:ID,baseIdentity:ID,runIdentity:ID,stdoutIdentity:ID,\nstderrIdentity:ID,ownerSid:SID,cwdMatches:true,plain:true,private:true,\nprofileAbsent:true,anchorRawBase64:string,intentRawBase64:string,\nnativeGateLineRawBase64:string}. Native rechecks actual current cwd, file identity,\nprivate ACL, plain ancestors and limits. Dart independently validates decoded raw\nbytes, original native prefix line, hash, own pid and C0 before MediaKit/Store.\n`startupValidationCloseGrantProof`: {protocol:1,attempt,rootScope:H,runIdentity:ID,\nfileIdentity:ID,plain:true,private:true,ownerMatches:true,rawBase64:string}.\nBase64 is standard RFC4648 alphabet, padding required, no whitespace. Decoded\nlimits follow anchor<=2048, intent<=8192, native line/grant<=4096. First method\nmust not derive a fresh proof from Dart arguments; second only reads fixed\nR/close.grant and never accepts caller path or observer completion assertion.\n\n## Additive native failure channel (Root approved 2026-11-26)\n\nNo existing C/phase/RPC/grant field or prior vector byte changes. Native also\nwrites `SHIYU_UI_FAILURE ` + canonical ASCII JSON + LF to the inherited private\nstderr handle. Whole line <=4096 bytes. This is auxiliary failure diagnostics,\nnever readiness, resource-release authority or a replacement C proof. A full\nfailure marker always makes the round sticky failed regardless of payload,\nincluding malformed payload or numeric error 0. Preserve raw bytes privately.\n\nClosed producer variants: {api:string,win32Code:uint32},\n{api:string,hresult:uint32}, {api:string,win32Code:uint32,cleanupFailures:array},\n{api:string,ntstatus:uint32,cleanupFailures:array}. No signed reinterpretation;\nuint32 is 0..4294967295. api is a source-fixed ASCII label, never error.message,\npath or VM URL. cleanup items are either {api:\"CloseHandle\",resource:fixed-label,\nwin32Code:uint32} or {api:\"CloseDesktop.input-query\",win32Code:uint32}.\nThese schema checks are audit-only: invalid fields never let a marker pass.\n\nOnly identifiable marker fragments count as partial protocol: at least the\n`SHIYU_UI_` namespace is required. Ordinary stderr tails such as `S` are ordinary\nlog bytes. An ambiguous namespace fragment delays ready without inventing a\ncomplete failure receipt; explicit `SHIYU_UI_F...` failure fragments fail sticky.\nPartial marker/JSON cannot grant readiness; identifiable terminal protocol\nfragments reject after real OS terminal. Read both logs by their pinned identity.\n",
